            <h3>Sand Section — Beachfront Manhattan Beach</h3>
            <p>The Sand Section is Manhattan Beach's defining neighborhood — the stretch of streets running west from Highland Avenue down to the Pacific Ocean, anchored by The Strand and the world-famous Manhattan Beach Pier. This is where Southern California's beach lifestyle reaches its most polished, most expensive, and most coveted expression. Properties here range from The Strand's iconic oceanfront homes to walk-street properties just steps from the sand, and the neighborhood's concentration of luxury residential real estate is among the densest in the country.</p>
            <p>The housing stock in the Sand Section runs from contemporary multi-story single-family homes to attached townhomes and luxury condominiums, with virtually every property having been substantially renovated or rebuilt in recent years. The Strand itself — the paved beachfront promenade that runs the length of the city — provides one of the most spectacular front-yard experiences in the world, and homes fronting directly onto it trade at prices that reflect this irreplaceable characteristic. Strand properties in Manhattan Beach regularly exceed $10 million, with some trades approaching $25 million for larger lots.</p>
            <p><strong>The Sand Section is where buyers come for the ultimate expression of Manhattan Beach luxury.</strong> Inventory is extremely limited, qualified buyers are abundant, and well-priced properties move decisively. Every transaction here requires sophisticated jumbo financing — often well into the multi-million dollar range — and having a lender with proven experience in high-value South Bay transactions is not optional.</p>
