            <h3>Tree Section — The Heart of Manhattan Beach</h3>
            <p>The Tree Section sits between the Sand Section to the west and Highland Avenue to the east, occupying the central residential core of Manhattan Beach. Named for the canopy of mature trees that line its streets — a deliberate choice by early city planners that has paid dividends for a century — the Tree Section is consistently cited as one of the most livable neighborhoods in the entire South Bay. It combines the best of everything: proximity to the beach and downtown, genuine walkability, community character, and homes that represent the full range of Manhattan Beach architectural expression from renovated original cottages to significant new construction.</p>
            <p>The Tree Section is also where the Manhattan Beach Greenbelt runs through the neighborhood — a long strip of park and walking path that bisects the area and provides a uniquely urban-pastoral amenity. Homes on or near the Greenbelt carry a premium. The Tree Section's proximity to Downtown Manhattan Beach — the restaurant and retail district centered on Manhattan Beach Boulevard — makes it one of the most walkable addresses in the beach cities.</p>
            <p><strong>The Tree Section is where many of Manhattan Beach's most sophisticated buyers ultimately land.</strong> It delivers beach proximity and walkability without the uncompromising price premium of The Strand, and its neighborhood character is difficult to replicate anywhere else in the South Bay. Homes here typically range from $2.5 million for a well-maintained original to $5 million or more for significant new construction.</p>
