            <p>The Hill Section occupies the elevated terrain just inland from the Sand Section, running north-south along the bluffs that overlook the Pacific Ocean. This geography gives the Hill Section something that most Manhattan Beach neighborhoods lack: elevation. From the Hill Section, many homes command sweeping panoramic views of the Pacific, Palos Verdes Peninsula, and on clear days, Catalina Island. The combination of ocean views, custom-built homes on larger lots, and proximity to both the beach and Downtown Manhattan Beach makes the Hill Section one of the most distinctive residential addresses in the South Bay.</p>
            <p>The housing stock in the Hill Section runs larger and more custom than most other Manhattan Beach neighborhoods. Homes here are typically single-family properties on 3,000 to 5,000 square foot lots, often with 3 to 4 bedrooms and 2 to 4 bathrooms, and more than 3,000 square feet of living space. Many have been substantially rebuilt or renovated to maximize their views and reflect contemporary luxury standards.</p>
            <p><strong>The Hill Section buyer values views, privacy, and custom architecture.</strong> At price points ranging from $3 million to well above $8 million for significant view properties, the Hill Section occupies the upper tier of the Manhattan Beach market. Jumbo financing with experience handling view property appraisals and high-value loan structures is essential.</p>
