            <p>East Manhattan Beach covers all areas east of Sepulveda Boulevard — the main dividing line through the city — and represents the most accessible entry point into Manhattan Beach real estate. Encompassing three distinct sub-neighborhoods (the Mira Costa District, Manhattan Heights/Liberty Village, and Manhattan Village), East Manhattan offers the full benefit of Manhattan Beach Unified School District, proximity to Mira Costa High School, and the community character of Manhattan Beach at price points that are meaningfully below the beachfront neighborhoods to the west.</p>
            <p>The Mira Costa District is the most prized part of East Manhattan, with 7,500 square foot lots — larger than virtually anywhere else in the city — that allow for substantial homes with yards. The Mira Costa area has attracted significant renovation and new construction activity as buyers recognize the value of the lot sizes and school district access. Manhattan Heights/Liberty Village offers a mix of original tract homes and updates at a modest entry price for the city. Both neighborhoods are within easy walking distance of Mira Costa High School, Manhattan Beach Middle School, and Polliwog Park.</p>
            <p><strong>East Manhattan Beach draws primarily families prioritizing school quality and buyers seeking the maximum square footage for their investment in the Manhattan Beach market.</strong> Price points here generally range from $1.5 million for modest originals to $4 million for large, fully renovated Mira Costa properties — still requiring significant jumbo financing but at a meaningful discount to the beachfront sections.</p>
