            <p>The housing stock within Manhattan Village consists primarily of single-family homes and attached townhomes, with the community's HOA providing maintenance of common areas, the security gates, and the community pools. The Mediterranean and Spanish Colonial architecture of many homes gives the community a consistent aesthetic character. Price points within Manhattan Village are generally more accessible than the beachfront sections but carry a premium over standard East Manhattan for the gated community benefits and amenities.</p>
            <p><strong>Manhattan Village attracts buyers who value security and community amenities alongside the Manhattan Beach school district and lifestyle.</strong> It is also popular with buyers relocating from gated communities in other cities who want to maintain that lifestyle while accessing the South Bay. HOA fees and the community's condominium-adjacent legal structure mean that financing here requires a lender familiar with gated community and PUD loan structures.</p>
